---
// src/pages/terms-and-conditions.astro
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Terms and Conditions | Luna Diving Thailand"
  description="Terms and Conditions for liveaboards, yacht charters, diving day trips, island tours and PADI courses booked with Luna Diving, Phuket, Thailand."
>
  <main class="legal-page">
    <article class="legal-content">
      <h1>Terms and Conditions</h1>
      <p class="legal-updated"><em>Last updated: October 2026</em></p>

      <p>
        These Terms and Conditions apply to all bookings made with <strong>Luna Diving Limited Partnership</strong>
        ("Luna Diving", "we", "us"), 27/15 Soi Pattana, Moo 4, Rawai, Phuket 83130, Thailand, licensed by the
        Tourism Authority of Thailand (TAT License No. 32/00034), and any person or entity who books a trip or
        service with us ("the customer", "you").
      </p>

      <h2>1. Scope</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms and Conditions define the contractual relationship between Luna Diving and the customer for all
        services booked through our website luna-diving-thailand.com, by WhatsApp, by email or in person, including
        liveaboard cruises, private yacht charters, diving day trips, island tours and PADI scuba diving courses.
      </p>
      <p>
        By confirming a booking, you accept these Terms and Conditions. They prevail over any other general or special
        conditions not expressly approved in writing by Luna Diving. We may update these Terms and Conditions at any
        time; the version in force on the date of your booking applies.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Services</h2>
      <p>
        The services we offer are those described on our website. Liveaboard cruises, yacht charters and some tours are
        operated by partner boat operators; Luna Diving acts as the booking agent and organiser of these services.
      </p>
      <p>
        Availability is limited and is confirmed only when we confirm your booking in writing. Descriptions and
        photographs are as accurate as possible, but boats, cabins, equipment and dive sites may differ slightly from
        the images shown.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Prices</h2>
      <p>
        Prices are shown in Thai Baht (THB) unless another currency is stated for a specific service. Unless otherwise
        indicated, prices are per person.
      </p>
      <p>
        What is included and not included is listed on the page of each service. Extra costs such as marine park fees,
        nitrox, equipment rental, alcoholic drinks and dive insurance are payable as described on that page, in some
        cases in cash on board.
      </p>

      <h2>4. How to Book</h2>
      <p>To book a service:</p>
      <ol>
        <li>
          Contact us through the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>, by WhatsApp or by email with your preferred
          dates, number of guests and diving certification level.
        </li>
        <li>We confirm availability and send you a booking confirmation with the total amount and payment details.</li>
        <li>Your booking is confirmed once we receive your payment as described in section 5.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>5. Payment</h2>
      <p>
        Full payment (100%) is required within 24–48 hours of the booking confirmation, unless a different deadline is
        stated in your confirmation.
      </p>
      <p>
        Payments are made by bank transfer in Thai Baht (THB) to the account indicated on your booking confirmation or
        invoice. The amount must be received net of all bank and transfer charges, which are paid by the customer.
      </p>
      <p>If payment is not received within the deadline, we may release the reserved places without further notice.</p>

      <h2>6. Cancellation and Changes</h2>
      <h3>Cancellation by the customer</h3>
      <p>Cancellations must be sent to us in writing (email or WhatsApp). The following charges apply:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>60 days or more before departure:</strong> 30% of the total price is retained.</li>
        <li><strong>Less than 60 days before departure:</strong> no refund.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        No refunds are given for unused services, late arrival, no-shows, or if a trip is shortened or interrupted for
        reasons beyond our control, including personal injury, illness, flight delays, mechanical breakdowns, weather and
        sea conditions, strikes, war, criminal acts, quarantine, or the emergency evacuation of another guest requiring
        the vessel to return to port.
      </p>

      <h3>Cancellation or changes by Luna Diving or the operator</h3>
      <p>
        If a trip is cancelled by Luna Diving or the operator before departure, we will offer you an equivalent
        alternative boat or date. If you do not accept the alternative, you will receive a full refund of the amount
        paid to us.
      </p>
      <p>
        Itineraries, dive sites and schedules may be changed without prior notice for reasons of safety, weather and sea
        conditions, national park regulations or other circumstances beyond our control. The captain and dive guides
        have the final decision on all matters of safety.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Travel and Dive Insurance</h2>
      <p>
        We strongly recommend that you purchase comprehensive travel insurance covering medical expenses, accidents,
        baggage, and trip cancellation and interruption at the time of booking. Luna Diving is not responsible for
        financial losses caused by events beyond our control that would normally be covered by such insurance.
      </p>
      <p>
        Dive accident insurance (such as DAN, PADI or equivalent) is mandatory for all certified divers on liveaboard
        trips and strongly recommended for all other diving activities.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Diving Requirements and Safety</h2>
      <p>Before diving, all divers must:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>complete and sign a liability release form and a medical questionnaire;</li>
        <li>
          show proof of their diving certification (or be enrolled in a PADI course or Discover Scuba Diving program);
        </li>
        <li>declare any medical condition that may affect their ability to dive.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Some dive sites and itineraries require a minimum certification level or recent diving experience, as indicated
        on the service page. Our dive guides may refuse or limit diving for any diver whose fitness, behaviour or skills
        may put their own safety or the safety of others at risk. In this case, no refund is due.
      </p>
      <p>
        Customers must follow the instructions of the crew and dive guides at all times, as well as the rules of the
        Thai national marine parks.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Liability</h2>
      <p>
        Luna Diving takes every reasonable care in organising your trip. As a booking agent for services operated by
        third parties, we are not liable for acts, omissions or defaults of boat operators, transport providers or other
        suppliers, beyond what is required by Thai law.
      </p>
      <p>
        We are not liable for damage resulting from the use of the internet, such as data loss, hacking, viruses or
        service interruptions.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Intellectual Property</h2>
      <p>
        All content on this website, including text, photographs, videos, logos and graphics, is the property of Luna
        Diving or of the boat operators who have authorised its use. It may not be copied, reproduced or used for
        commercial purposes without our written permission.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Personal data you provide when booking is used only to manage your booking and to contact you about your trip.
        Please see our <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a> for details.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Governing Law and Disputes</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms and Conditions are governed by the laws of the Kingdom of Thailand. Any dispute shall be submitted to
        the competent courts of Phuket, Thailand.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <address class="legal-contact">
        Luna Diving Limited Partnership<br />
        27/15 Soi Pattana, Moo 4, Rawai, Phuket 83130, Thailand<br />
        Email: <a href="mailto:info@luna-diving-thailand.com">info@luna-diving-thailand.com</a><br />
        WhatsApp: <a href="https://wa.me/66918233120" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">+66 91 823 3120</a><br />
        TAT License No. 32/00034
      </address>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    width: 100%;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    padding: clamp(110px, 12vw, 150px) 20px 80px;
    background: #ffffff;
    color: #1a1a1a;
    font-family: 'Inter', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
  }

  .legal-content {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0 0 8px;
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 4vw, 2.6rem);
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .legal-updated {
    margin: 0 0 32px;
    color: #706f6f;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 40px 0 12px;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  h3 {
    margin: 24px 0 8px;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  p {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    color: #3a3a3a;
  }

  ul,
  ol {
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    padding-left: 22px;
    color: #3a3a3a;
  }

  li {
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }

  a {
    color: #008ea7;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  a:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid #008ea7;
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .legal-contact {
    font-style: normal;
    color: #3a3a3a;
  }
</style>
